X: offertory
L: Secreta
 = Secret
T: ^CONCEDE, quǽsumus Dómine, ut óculis tuæ majestátis munus oblátum, et grátiam nobis devotiónis obtíneat, et efféctum beátæ perennitátis acquírat. Per Dóminum.
 = Grant, we beseech You, O Lord, that this gift, offered in the presence of Your majesty, may obtain for us the grace of devotion, and bring us to everlasting joys: through our Lord.
R: Præfatio *Qui salútem humáni.*
 = Preface *Qui salútem humáni* (of the Cross).
X: offertoryEnd, pref, sa, canon
T: {Communio Matth. 26} Pater, si non potest hic calix transíre nisi bibam illum, fiat volúntas tua.
 = {Communion Matt. 26} Father, if this cup cannot pass away unless I drink it, Your will be done.
C: co 0
X: post
L: Postcommunio
 = Postcommunion
T: ^PER hujus, Dómine, operatiónem mystérii, et vítia nostra purgéntur; et justa desidéria compleántur : Per Dóminum.
 = By virtue of this mystery, O Lord, may our sins be cleansed and our just desires be fulfilled: through our Lord.
R: Si Missa privata legitur, in fine dicatur Evangelium *Cum appropinquásset Jesus,* ut supra in benedictione Palmarum, pag. 139
 = If the Mass is said privately, the Gospel *Cum appropinquásset Jesus* is said at the end, as above at the blessing of the Palms, p. 139.
